# Brand Voice — Midnight Magnolia

## Voice anchors
- **Audre Lorde** clarity — name the thing without softening it
- **Bernice McFadden** tenderness — meet the reader where they are
- **Beyoncé** restraint — say less, mean more

Plain-spoken. Southern. Black literary. Never breathless, never hustle-coded.

## Do / Don't

| Do | Don't |
|---|---|
| "Taken seriously" | "Transform your life" |
| "Walked into the world" | "Unleash your potential" |
| "Editorial work" | "Level up your manuscript" |
| "Done together" | "Crush your goals" |
| "Find out if we're the right fit" | "Book your dream session today" |
| Plain present tense | All-caps urgency |
| Specific outcomes ("live on Amazon") | Vague aspiration ("amazing results") |
| Soft authority | Hustle pressure |

## When drafting copy
1. Lead with the **outcome** in plain language
2. Name the **fear or hesitation** the reader is holding
3. Use **specific** verbs ("walked," "carried," "moved") not generic ones ("get," "achieve")
4. **No em-dashes-as-drama**. Em-dashes used sparingly, for the rhythm Lorde used them for.
5. **No emojis** in copy unless the user explicitly asks
6. Always offer **primary + 2–3 alternates** so the user can pick the rhythm

## Forbidden phrases
"unlock," "transform," "level up," "10x," "crush it," "game-changer," "no-brainer," "elevate," "synergy," "ecosystem of solutions"

